<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hugh of Arles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 880–948</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Hugh of Provence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hugh of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arles">Arles</a>, also called Hugh of Provence, was count of Arles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> and effective ruler of Provence before becoming King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 926. He sought to control <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> through marriage to Marozia but was driven out by her son Alberic II in 932. In 933 he gave up his rights in Provence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-of-burgundy">Rudolf II of Upper Burgundy</a>, uniting the two Burgundies. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-ii-of-italy">Berengar of Ivrea</a> later forced him from power, and he died in Provence in 948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles.jpg" alt="Hugh of Arles" width="320" height="658" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugh_of_Italy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
